ity before applying a lesson.', 'title': 'Timing Failure Needs Fresher Entry'}, {'confirmation_required': ['strong_m1_momentum', 'momentum_alignment', 'directional_impulse'], 'failed_when': ['momentum was weak', 'momentum was mixed', 'price drifted without impulse'], 'id': 'momentum_must_confirm', 'lesson': 'Mixed M1 momentum is not enough for a continuation setup after recent losses. Atlas should wait for strong or clearly turning momentum before treating the setup as corrected.', 'teaching_action': 'Do not repeat weak-momentum entries; wait until momentum confirms the same side.', 'title': 'Momentum Must Confirm'}, {'confirmation_required': ['structure_hold', 'clear_structure', 'not_mid_range'], 'failed_when': ['structure was unclear', 'structure did not hold', 'price was mid-range without a clean reaction'], 'id': 'structure_must_hold', 'lesson': 'Structure labels like HH/HL or LH/LL are not enough by themselves. Atlas needs evidence that structure is holding at the entry location before execution review.', 'teaching_action': 'Treat unclear structure as developing context, not execution permission.', 'title': 'Structure Must Hold'}, {'confirmation_required': ['failed_ingredient_corrected', 'current_setup_differs_from_loss_memory', 'normal_gates_still_pass'], 'failed_when': ['same pattern is repeated with the same missing evidence', 'loss memory is interpreted as a blanket ban', 'confidence is punished without a correction path'], 'id': 'loss_pattern_is_not_pattern_ban', 'lesson': 'A loss in a pattern does not mean Atlas must stop trading that pattern. It means Atlas must identify what failed and require a corrected version before trading it again.', 'teaching_action': 'Keep the pattern tradable, but require proof that the previous mistake is not being repeated.', 'title': 'Loss Pattern Is Not Pattern Ban'}, {'confirmation_required': ['manual_operator_review_for_unlock', 'risk_guard_clear', 'strategy_learning_explained_separately'], 'failed_when': ['risk protection is confused with pattern learning', 'operator assumes safety lock means strategy ban', 'Atlas explains safety as if it were setup logic'], 'id': 'safety_lock_is_separate_from_learning', 'lesson': 'The safety lock protects the account after weak performance. It is not a lesson that a setup family should never trade again.', 'teaching_action': 'Explain safety lock and pattern learning as separate lanes.', 'title': 'Safety Lock Is Separate From Learning'}], 'policy_note': 'These teachings are bounded knowledge and observability. They do not rewrite strategies, lower thresholds, alter risk, unlock safety, force entries, or bypass execution gates.', 'relevant': [{'confirmation_required': ['fresh_entry_location', 'retest_or_pullback', 'no_overextension'], 'failed_when': ['entry chased expansion', 'entry arrived before confirmation', 'entry was mid-range or stale'], 'id': 'timing_failure_needs_fresher_entry', 'lesson': 'When the idea was possibly valid but timing was early, late, or weak, Atlas should not discard the idea. It should wait for a fresher entry, retest, pullback, or cleaner trigger.', 'teaching_action': 'Separate idea quality from entry timing quality before applying a lesson.', 'title': 'Timing Failure Needs Fresher Entry'}], 'schema_version': 1}, 'enabled': True, 'historical_loss_teachings': {'clusters': [{'confirmation_required': ['rejection_after_sweep', 'structure_reclaim', 'momentum_confirmation', 'fresh_entry_location'], 'dominant_context': {'momentum': 'weak_or_unknown', 'regime': 'trend', 'session': 'other', 'setup_family': 'unknown', 'side': 'buy'}, 'dominant_strategies': ['momentum_continuation', 'evolved_rule'], 'id': 'broad_buy_timing_stop_hunt_cluster', 'lesson': 'Many losing buy attempts came from weakly described trend contexts where timing was vulnerable to stop-hunts. Atlas should not read this as a buy ban; it should require evidence that the entry is not just the first push into liquidity.', 'loss_count': 54, 'teaching_action': 'When a similar buy pattern appears, classify it as developing until the chart proves rejection/reclaim and fresh momentum instead of repeating the same weak timing.', 'title': 'Broad Buy Timing Stop-Hunt Cluster'}, {'confirmation_required': ['defined_reaction_zone', 'structure_hold_or_reclaim', 'same_side_support', 'no_mid_range_chase'], 'dominant_context': {'momentum': 'weak_or_unknown', 'regime': 'trend_or_range', 'session': 'other', 'setup_family': 'unknown', 'side': 'sell'}, 'dominant_strategies': ['evolved_rule', 'momentum_continuation'], 'id': 'broad_sell_timing_stop_hunt_cluster', 'lesson': 'The sell-side losses also point to timing vulnerability, especially when setup family and location were not known. Atlas should avoid treating a directional sell bias as execution permission without a clean reaction point.', 'loss_count': 27, 'teaching_action': 'When a similar sell pattern appears, keep it tradable but require the missing reaction/location evidence before execution review.', 'title': 'Broad Sell Timing Stop-Hunt Cluster'}, {'confirmation_required': ['strong_m1_momentum', 'structure_hold', 'avoid_first_push', 'execution_friction_acceptable'], 'dominant_context': {'momentum': 'mixed_to_strong', 'regime': 'trend', 'session': 'new_york_or_london', 'setup_family': 'continuation', 'volatility': 'normal_to_high'}, 'dominant_strategies': ['evolved_rule', 'momentum_continuation', 'gold_micro_impulse'], 'id': 'false_continuation_confirmation_cluster', 'lesson': 'Continuation losses were not teaching Atlas to stop trading continuation. They were teaching that continuation needs structure to hold after the first push, momentum in the trade direction, and friction checks before entry.', 'loss_count': 12, 'teaching_action': 'Trade continuation again only when the failed confirmation ingredient is corrected and existing gates still pass.', 'title': 'False Continuation Confirmation Cluster'}, {'confirmation_required': ['spread_liquidity_acceptable', 'slippage_state_known_or_safe'